  "title": "review: fix round 3 (review): S2f2 steering_policy in shadow: deterministic triggers (dependency merged, stuck, out-of-s",
  "spec": "Fix round 3 for T-1274: review T-1304 requested changes. fix round 3: address review T-1304 comment orchestrator/decision_log.py:263 [med]: Grouped recent() only stops early once every subject has an applied row. In shadow mode, and for any task that has never been steered, no applied row exists. So the scan runs backwards through the entire decisions.jsonl every tick, and the tick cost still grows with total log size, which is the review's complaint. The `limit` argument (limit=2 from steering_tick) is also ignored in grouped mode, s fix round 3: address review T-1304 comment orchestrator/daemon.py:1676 [low]: steering_refusal_reasons is only updated while mode is active. If the config goes active, then shadow or off, then active again with the same refusal reasons, the stale remembered reasons suppress the notification. Reset it when mode is not active. fix round 3: address review T-1304 comment orchestrator/steering_policy.py:33 [low]: safe_scope falls back to Path('.') (the process cwd) when neither a worktree argument nor task['worktree'] is set. Containment is then checked against the daemon's cwd rather than a task worktree. It is harmless in practice, but the fallback is implicit. Return the entries unchanged, or skip the check, when no worktree is known. fix round 3 rule: decision_log.recent grouped mode must be bounded: scan at most limit rows per subject from the end (limit honoured) and stop after a fixed maximum of rows read (for example 2000) regardless of whether applied rows were found; with subjects empty return immediately without reading. Reset the remembered steering_refusal_reasons whenever the mode is not active so a later return to active notifies again. safe_scope returns the entries unchanged when no worktree is known (no cwd fallback). Run .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh . until it exits 0; do not ask questions; report files changed and failures-only output.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1305"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_steering_policy.py::test_triggers_in_order_and_actions (each trigger from fixtures yields the documented action and message)",
    "tests/test_steering_policy.py::test_min_interval_and_critical_path_rule",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_tick_records_steering_rows_in_shadow_without_calling_worker_control",
    "tests/test_promotion.py::test_steering_policy_feature_registered",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_active_steering_calls_once_respects_interval_and_logs_errors",
    "tests/test_pool.py::test_steering_section_defaults_and_invalid_mode_falls_back",
    "tests/test_decision_log.py::test_steering_rows_omit_message_text",
    "tests/test_steering_policy.py::test_git_status_rules_timeout_and_ignored_paths",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_active_mode_never_cancels_and_skips_in_flight_steers",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh exits 0",
    "fix round 3: address review T-1304 comment orchestrator/decision_log.py:263 [med]: Grouped recent() only stops early once every subject has an applied row. In shadow mode, and for any task that has never been steered, no applied row exists. So the scan runs backwards through the entire decisions.jsonl every tick, and the tick cost still grows with total log size, which is the review's complaint. The `limit` argument (limit=2 from steering_tick) is also ignored in grouped mode, s",
    "fix round 3: address review T-1304 comment orchestrator/daemon.py:1676 [low]: steering_refusal_reasons is only updated while mode is active. If the config goes active, then shadow or off, then active again with the same refusal reasons, the stale remembered reasons suppress the notification. Reset it when mode is not active.",
    "fix round 3: address review T-1304 comment orchestrator/steering_policy.py:33 [low]: safe_scope falls back to Path('.') (the process cwd) when neither a worktree argument nor task['worktree'] is set. Containment is then checked against the daemon's cwd rather than a task worktree. It is harmless in practice, but the fallback is implicit. Return the entries unchanged, or skip the check, when no worktree is known.",
    "fix round 3 rule: decision_log.recent grouped mode must be bounded: scan at most limit rows per subject from the end (limit honoured) and stop after a fixed maximum of rows read (for example 2000) regardless of whether applied rows were found; with subjects empty return immediately without reading. Reset the remembered steering_refusal_reasons whenever the mode is not active so a later return to active notifies again. safe_scope returns the entries unchanged when no worktree is known (no cwd fallback)."
  ],
